{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The expression for $f(x)$ includes an exponential term.\n\nRemember that the derivative of the general exponential term $a^x$ (where $a$ is any positive constant) is $\\ln(a)\\cdot a^x$.\n\nPut another way, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(a^x)=\\ln(a)\\cdot a^x$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-8\\cdot7^x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\dfrac{d}{dx}(7^x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\cdot\\ln(7)\\cdot7^x\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-8\\cdot7^x\\ln(7)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $f'(x)=-8\\cdot7^x\\ln(7)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=-8\\cdot7^x$.\n\n**Find $f'(x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-8\\cdot 7^x\\ln(7)$","correct":true},{"content":"$-56^{x-1}$","correct":false},{"content":"$-8\\cdot 7^x\\log_7(x)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$-8\\cdot 7^{x-1}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
